<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Binding Picture Showcase</title>
<style>
:root { --bg: #ffffff; --fg: #1b1f24; --muted: #57606a; --line: #d0d7de; --accent: #0b5cad;
  --warn: #9a6700; --ok: #1a7f37; --bad: #cf222e; --quote: #f6f8fa; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root { --bg: #0d1117; --fg: #e6edf3; --muted: #8d96a0; --line: #30363d; --accent: #58a6ff;
    --warn: #d29922; --ok: #3fb950; --bad: #f85149; --quote: #161b22; }
}
body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font: 16px/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif;
  margin: 0 auto; max-width: 72rem; padding: 0 16px 4rem; }
h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; } h2 { margin-top: 3rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
.question { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
.muted { color: var(--muted); }
table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.92rem; display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
th, td { border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0.35rem 0.5rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
.undeclared { color: var(--warn); font-weight: 600; }
.PASSED, .MATCHED, .COVERED, .RESOLVED, .SUPPORTS, .JUSTIFIED { color: var(--ok); font-weight: 600; }
.FAILED, .DIFFERENT, .MISSING, .INCOMPLETE, .NOT_CITED, .DOES_NOT_SUPPORT, .UNRESOLVED, .UNJUSTIFIED { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 600; }
.agent { background: var(--quote); border-left: 3px solid var(--line); margin: 0.3rem 0; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; display: block; white-space: pre-wrap; }
code { font-size: 0.88em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Before an AI agent changes a distributed system, do we understand the bindings that change relies on?</h1>
<p>Sokol111 is a multi-tenant e-commerce system. Its services exchange events through a Redpanda
broker. The modernization step shown here moves one bounded context, Catalog Management (the Catalog
and Image services), to Apache Kafka, with MirrorMaker 2 bridging the two brokers. A move like this is
safe only if every binding that crosses the boundary of the moving context is known before the move
and still holds after it.</p>
<p>The flow of this page follows that question. First the bindings, then what is declared and what
the evidence establishes, then the plan that a coding agent built on that picture, then what the
evidence establishes after the move. AIP is read-only: it gives understanding of the bindings, not
power over the system.</p>

<h2>1. Before: the boundary and the bindings that cross it</h2>
<p class="question">(1) What boundary changes?</p>
<p>Catalog Management moves from Redpanda (<code>kafka:sokol111-local</code>) to Apache Kafka
(<code>kafka:sokol111-kafka</code>). Store Provisioning (Tenant) and Storefront (Product Query,
Category Query) stay on Redpanda. Before the move, only Redpanda has a capture.</p>
<p class="question">(2) Which relationships cross it?</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Consumer</th><th>Topic</th><th>Crossing</th><th>Status</th><th>Consumer groups</th></tr>
{% for row in before_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ row.get("consumer_service_id") | service }}</td><td><code>{{ row.topic_name }}</code></td>
<td>{{ row.crossing }}</td>
<td{% if row.get("reason") == "PROMISE_COVERAGE_MISSING" %} class="undeclared"{% endif %}>{{ row.status }}{% if row.get("reason") %} / {{ row.get("reason") }}{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ row.group_ids | join(", ") }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="muted">Each row is one consumer Service, Topic and broker at the capture time. Limitations
of this answer: {{ before_limitations | join(", ") }}.</p>

<h2>2. Insight: what is declared, and what the evidence establishes</h2>
<p class="question">(3) Which bindings are declared, which are observed, and which are unresolved?</p>
<p>The documented architecture says that Catalog Management publishes product and category events to
the storefront. The broker evidence shows more. The rows marked <span class="undeclared">observed,
undeclared</span> are bindings that no document names: the moving services consume tenant events
from Store Provisioning, and the storefront consumes attribute events from Catalog Management. A
move planned from the documents alone would not bridge them.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Binding</th><th>Declared (catalog)</th><th>Resolved Topic</th><th>Observed attachment</th><th>Evidence refs</th></tr>
{% for row in before_rows if row.crossing in ("INBOUND", "OUTBOUND") %}
<tr><td>{{ row.get("consumer_service_id") | service }} &times; <code>{{ row.topic_name }}</code></td>
<td>{% if row.get("reason") == "PROMISE_COVERAGE_MISSING" %}<span class="undeclared">none: observed, undeclared</span>{% else %}promised: {{ row.declared_event_types | join(", ") or "-" }}{% endif %}</td>
<td><code>{{ row.get("topic_id") or "-" }}</code></td>
<td>{{ row.group_ids | join(", ") or "none" }}{% if row.get("captured_at") %} at {{ row.get("captured_at") }}{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ (row.promise_evidence_refs | length) }} promise, {{ (row.attachment_evidence_refs | length) }} attachment, {{ (row.mapping_evidence_refs | length) }} mapping</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="muted">An attachment establishes that a consumer group was attached to the topic at the
capture time. It does not establish which event types the consumer handles, or an end-to-end event
flow.</p>

<h2>3. Agent: why the bindings matter for this move</h2>
<p class="question">(4) Why do they matter for the migration?</p>
<p>A coding agent planned and carried out the move. It read the binding picture through AIP's MCP
interface. AIP establishes the bindings. The agent derives the migration requirements, then chooses
and carries out the plan. Independent evidence establishes what the migration achieved.</p>
<p>Each chain below starts from a binding that crosses the boundary after the move and ends with the
check that is independent of AIP. The agent's own words are quoted.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Observed binding (AIP)</th><th>Migration requirement</th><th>Agent decision</th><th>Independent verification</th></tr>
{% for chain in chains %}
<tr>
<td>{{ chain.consumer }} &times; <code>{{ chain.row.topic_name }}</code> on {{ chain.broker }}: {{ chain.row.crossing }}, {{ chain.row.status }}{% if chain.continues %}<br><span class="muted">before: {{ chain.continues.status }} on Redpanda</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td>{% if chain.key %}{{ chain.key.requirement }} <span class="muted">({{ chain.key.id }})</span>{% else %}-{% endif %}</td>
<td>Proof A <span class="{{ chain.proof_a }}">{{ chain.proof_a }}</span>, Proof B <span class="{{ chain.proof_b }}">{{ chain.proof_b }}</span>
{% for item in chain.plan_items %}
<span class="agent">{{ item.id }}: {{ item.action }}{% for j in item.implementation_justification %} · [{{ j.kind }}] {{ j.reference }}{% endfor %}</span>
{% endfor %}</td>
<td>replication: {{ chain.verification.replication | join(", ") }}<br>lag: {{ chain.verification.lag | join(", ") }}<br>functional test: {{ chain.verification.functional }}</td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h3>Proof A: the plan against the answer key</h3>
<p>The answer key was frozen before the agent run. The agent did not see it.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Key item</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Plan items</th><th>Recorded reason</th></tr>
{% for result in scoring.key_items %}
<tr><td>{{ result.id }}</td><td class="{{ result.verdict }}">{{ result.verdict }}</td><td>{{ result.plan_items | join(", ") }}</td><td>{{ result.reason or "" }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% for entry in scoring.owner_judged %}
<tr><td>{{ entry.id }}: {{ entry.check }}</td><td class="{{ entry.verdict }}">{{ entry.verdict }}</td><td>{{ entry.plan_items | join(", ") }}</td><td>{{ entry.reason or "" }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p>Plan items that no key item claims: {{ scoring.extra | join(", ") or "none" }}.</p>

<h3>Proof B: the AIP claims the plan cites</h3>
<p>A pass means that the binding behind a plan item is evidenced. It never means that the action is
correct; the mechanism is checked by the broker tools and the functional test.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Key item</th><th>Coverage</th><th>Missing rows</th></tr>
{% for c in citations.coverage %}
<tr><td>{{ c.id }}</td><td class="{{ c.verdict }}">{{ c.verdict }}</td><td>{% for r in c.missing_rows %}{{ r[2] | service }} &times; {{ r[1] }}<br>{% endfor %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p>Mechanism items without an implementation justification: {{ citations.unjustified | join(", ") or "none" }}.
Citations that did not resolve: {{ citations.unresolved | join(", ") or "none" }}.</p>

<h3>The plan, item by item, with the AIP claims each item cites</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Plan item</th><th>AIP claims cited (resolution, support)</th><th>Implementation justification</th></tr>
{% for checked in citations["items"] %}
{% set item = plan_items_by_id[checked.id] %}
<tr><td><span class="agent">{{ item.id }}: {{ item.action }}</span></td>
<td>{% for c in checked.citations %}{% for r in c.rows %}{{ r[2] | service }} &times; <code>{{ r[1] }}</code> {% endfor %}{% if not c.rows %}<code>{{ c.citation | tojson }}</code> {% endif %}<span class="{{ c.resolution }}">{{ c.resolution }}</span>{% if c.support is defined %}, <span class="{{ c.support }}">{{ c.support }}</span>{% endif %}<br>{% else %}none{% endfor %}</td>
<td><span class="{{ checked.justification }}">{{ checked.justification }}</span>{% for j in item.implementation_justification %}<span class="agent">[{{ j.kind }}] {{ j.reference }}{% if j.get("note") %}: {{ j.note }}{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h3>The agent's plan, as written</h3>
<blockquote class="agent">{{ plan_md }}</blockquote>
{% if amendments %}
<h3>Amendments made while carrying out the plan</h3>
{% for a in amendments %}
<blockquote class="agent">{{ a.utc }} {{ a.change }} {{ a.item_id }}: {{ a.reason }}</blockquote>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<h2>4. After: the binding picture on both brokers</h2>
<p class="question">(5) What does the evidence after the move establish?</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Broker</th><th>Consumer</th><th>Topic</th><th>Crossing</th><th>Status</th><th>Consumer groups</th></tr>
{% for row in after_rows %}
<tr><td>{{ row.broker_id | broker }}</td><td>{{ row.get("consumer_service_id") | service }}</td><td><code>{{ row.topic_name }}</code></td><td>{{ row.crossing }}</td>
<td{% if row.get("reason") == "PROMISE_COVERAGE_MISSING" %} class="undeclared"{% endif %}>{{ row.status }}{% if row.get("reason") %} / {{ row.get("reason") }}{% endif %}</td>
<td>{{ row.group_ids | join(", ") }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p class="muted">Limitations of this answer: {{ after_limitations | join(", ") }}. Each broker keeps its own
Topic ids; AIP does not merge them and does not establish delivery across the brokers.</p>
{% if gone %}
<p>No live attachment here after the move (a comparison of the two captures, not a detachment claim
beyond them):</p>
<ul>
{% for row in gone %}<li>{{ row.get("consumer_service_id") | service }} &times; <code>{{ row.topic_name }}</code> on {{ row.broker_id | broker }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endif %}

<p>Proof C, the after-wave answer against the reference frozen before the run
(<code>expected-after.json</code>): <span class="{{ proof_c.result }}">{{ proof_c.result }}</span>.</p>

<h3>External checks, apart from AIP's claims</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Check</th><th>Established by</th><th>Result</th></tr>
{% for v in replication %}<tr><td>replication caught up: {{ v.partitions | map(attribute="topic") | unique | join(", ") }}</td><td>broker tools</td><td class="{{ v.result }}">{{ v.result }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
{% for v in lag %}<tr><td>consumer lag 0: {{ v.group }}</td><td>broker tools</td><td class="{{ v.result }}">{{ v.result }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
<tr><td>offset hand-off (installed offset as reported by the agent; the operator's later reads beside it)</td><td>broker tools and the agent's transcript</td><td class="{{ handoff.result }}">{{ handoff.result }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>applied MirrorMaker 2 configuration</td><td>the operator's reading of the running containers</td><td class="{{ applied_mm2.result }}">{{ applied_mm2.result }}</td></tr>
<tr><td>applied Catalog and Image configuration</td><td>the operator's reading of the ConfigMaps</td><td class="{{ applied_helm.result }}">{{ applied_helm.result }}</td></tr>
{% for s in functional_test.steps %}<tr><td>functional test {{ s.step }}</td><td>the services' Connect-RPC endpoints</td><td class="{{ s.result }}">{{ s.result }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<table>
<tr><th>Hand-off entry</th><th>(a) final offset on Redpanda</th><th>(c) installed on Kafka</th><th>Checkpoint matches</th><th>Kafka position now</th><th>Replay amount</th></tr>
{% for e in handoff.entries %}
<tr><td>{{ e.group }} {{ e.topic }}-{{ e.partition }}</td><td>{{ e.a.value }}</td><td>{{ e.c.value }} <span class="muted">({{ e.c.source }})</span></td>
<td>{{ e.checkpoint_matches }}</td><td>{{ e.kafka_position_now.value }}</td><td>{{ e.replay.kind }}{% if e.replay.records is defined %}: {{ e.replay.records }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>Proof boundaries</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Claim</th><th>Established by</th></tr>
<tr><td>group state and topic assignments per broker, before and after, attributed to Services</td><td>AIP</td></tr>
<tr><td>offsets, lag, replication progress</td><td>broker tools (<code>rpk</code>, <code>kafka-consumer-groups</code>), stored as ground truth</td></tr>
<tr><td>the migrated behaviour works</td><td>the functional test after the cut-over</td></tr>
</table>
<p>What an instrument measures is not what people conclude from it. Each claim on this page names
the instrument that establishes it.</p>

<h2>How the agent run was kept independent</h2>
<ul>
<li>Agent: {{ agent.model }} in Claude Code {{ agent.claude_code_version }}.</li>
<li>The agent saw a task card with the goal and the safety constraints only (SHA-256 <code>{{ agent.task_card_sha256 }}</code>). It did not see the answer key, the reference runbook, the specifications or the web.</li>
<li>The plan was frozen at {{ agent.plan_frozen_at }} (SHA-256 <code>{{ agent.plan_sha256 }}</code>), before the first command that changed the environment.</li>
<li>Transcript audit: {% if audit.clean %}no hit{% else %}{{ audit.hits | length }} hit(s), each a waived environment fault that exposed nothing withheld, with its evidence in the run record{% endif %}.</li>
<li>Operator interventions for environment faults: {% if agent.interventions %}{{ agent.interventions | length }}, listed in the run record{% else %}none{% endif %}.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Disclosures</h2>
<ul>
<li>The EventCatalog and its owners are generated for the showcase from Sokol111's two architecture documents by a fixed rule. Its entries count as confirmed promises by assumption; they are not promises that the service teams made.</li>
<li>The topic inventory, the producer and Service declarations and the consumer group to Service mapping are authored from source and configuration.</li>
<li>The second broker and the bridge are authored for the showcase: a local Apache Kafka stands in for a managed platform, and Sokol111 itself runs one Redpanda broker.</li>
<li>Local adaptations, none committed to a Sokol111 repository: MinIO from frozen Bitnami images, Logto pinned by digest, the k3d host adaptations, a host DNS workaround, and the Logto seed run a second time.</li>
<li>The agent, its task card and its sessions are described above. The answer key is the authors' expected plan, written before the run.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Evaluate it on your own architecture</h2>
<p>This page shows one move in one system. The question it asks applies to any change that crosses a
boundary: which bindings cross it, which are declared, and what the evidence establishes before and
after. We invite you to ask that question of your own architecture with AIP.</p>
</body>
</html>
